[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS010
TITLE: Issue or refuse takeoff clearance
STATEMENT: >>>
The Tower CSCI shall issue a takeoff clearance only when the aircraft is at the head of a departure-capable runway sequence and the separation guard accepts the transition into the protected volume or through it to airborne. Otherwise it shall refuse. The issued clearance shall name the aircraft, the runway, and the wind from the airport configuration when wind is present. Acceptance is a head aircraft on a departure runway that is cleared, and a second aircraft on that runway that is refused.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Takeoff is one of the FAA tower clearances and it is also an occupancy transition.
<<<
DAL: A
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: High-Level
VERIFICATION: Test
ASSUMPTIONS: The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.
